./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37971:20.223 fo:text-align
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37975:If there are no values specified for the fo:text-align and style:justify-single-word 20.301 attributes within the same formatting properties element, the values of those attributes is set to start and false respectively.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37977:In the OpenDocument XSL-compatible namespace, the fo:text-align attribute does not support the inherit, inside, outside, or string values.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37979:The fo:text-align attribute is usable with the following elements: <style:list-level-properties> 17.19 and <style:paragraph-properties> 17.6.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37981:The values of the fo:text-align attribute are start, end, left, right, center or justify.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37985:The fo:text-align attribute when used with the <style:paragraph-properties> 17.6 element specifies the alignment of text in a paragraph. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37989:The fo:text-align attribute is usable with the following element: <style:paragraph-properties> 17.6.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37991:The values of the fo:text-align attribute are start, end, left, right, center or justify.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37995:The fo:text-align attribute when used with the <style:list-level-properties> 17.20 element specifies the alignment of list labels. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37997:If the text:list-level-position-and-space-mode 20.431 attribute on the same <style:list-level-properties> element has the value label-width-and-position, the fo:text-align attribute specifies the horizontal alignment of the list label within the width specified by the text:min-label-width 20.433 attribute. If the actual width of the list label is greater than the specified minimum width no alignment takes place.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37999:If the text:list-level-position-and-space-mode attribute on the same <style:list-level-properties> element has the value label-alignment, the value of the text:min-label-width attribute is treated as 0 and the fo:text-align attribute specifies the horizontal alignment of the list label at the alignment position. The alignment position is specified by the fo:margin-left 20.207 and fo:text-indent 20.225 attributes of its child element <style:list-level-label-alignment> 17.20.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38001:The defined values for the fo:text-align attribute are:
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38005:•end: interpreted as fo:text-align=”right” 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38013:•start: interpreted as fo:text-align=”left”. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38015:The fo:text-align attribute is usable with the following element: <style:list-level-properties> 17.19.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38017:The values of the fo:text-align attribute are start, end, left, right, center or justify.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38019:20.224 fo:text-align-last
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38023:This attribute is ignored if it not accompanied by an fo:text-align 20.223 attribute.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38027:The fo:text-align-last attribute is usable with the following element: <style:paragraph-properties> 17.6.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38029:The values of the fo:text-align-last attribute are start, center or justify.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38539:20.254 style:column-width
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38541:The style:column-width attribute specifies a fixed width for a column.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38543:The style:column-width attribute is usable with the following element: <style:table-column-properties> 17.16.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38545:The style:column-width attribute has the data type positiveLength 18.3.27.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38549:The fo:margin-bottom 20.206 attribute of a paragraph and the fo:margin-top 20.209 attribute of the next paragraph are ignored, so that the space between the paragraphs is zero, if all of the following conditions hold:
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38891:•true: line height is calculated only from the font height as specified by the font size attributes fo:font-size 20.190, style:font-size-asian 20.284 and style:font-size-complex 20.285. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39375:1)Values of attributes fo:border-top 20.183.6, fo:border-bottom 20.183.3, fo:border-left 20.183.4 and fo:border-right 20.183.5 are the same. These values can also be given by the fo:border 20.183.2 attribute. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39379:3)Values of attributes fo:padding-left 20.219 and fo:padding-right 20.220 are the same. These values can also be given by the fo:padding 20.217 attribute. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39381:4)Values of the fo:margin-right 20.208 attributes are the same. These values can also be given by the fo:margin 20.205 attribute. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39383:5)Values of the fo:margin-left 20.207 attribute, which can also be given by the fo:margin, and fo:text-indent 19.246 attributes, that meet one of these conditions: 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39386:2.Values of the fo:margin-left attributes are the same and values of the fo:text-indent attributes are non-negative. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39388:3.Value of the fo:margin-left attribute of one paragraph whose value of the fo:text-indent attribute is non-negative is the same as the sum of values of the fo:margin-left and fo:text-indent attributes of the other paragraph whose value of the fo:text-indent attribute is negative. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39390:4.Both values of the fo:text-indent attributes are negative and the sums of values of the fo:margin-left and fo:text-indent attributes are equal. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39408:Specifying a style:justify-single-word attribute without specifying a fo:text-align 20.223 and fo:text-align-last 20.224 attribute has no effect. Unspecified, both fo:text-align and fo:text-align-last have the value start.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:40360:•fix: content alignment uses the value of the fo:text-align 20.223 attribute. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41049:20.399 style:width
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41051:The style:width attribute specifies the fixed width of a table. Every table shall have a fixed width. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41053:The style:width attribute is usable with the following element: <style:table-properties> 17.15.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41055:The style:width attribute has the data type positiveLength 18.3.27.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41267:If the fo:text-align with value start, text alignment can be adapted to the writing mode.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41641:•label-alignment: The <style:list-level-label-alignment> 17.20 element and the fo:text-align 20.223 attribute are used to define the position and spacing of the list label and the list item. The values of the attributes for text:space-before 20.435, text:min-label-width 20.433 and text:min-label-distance 20.432 are assumed to be 0. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41643:•label-width-and-position: The text:space-before, text:min-label-width, text:min-label-distance and fo:text-align attributes are used to define the position and spacing of the list label and the list item. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41671:The list label can be aligned horizontally within the specified minimum width using the fo:text-align 20.223 attribute. If the actual width of the list label is greater than the specified minimum width no alignment takes place.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41753:•false: paragraph style determines position of tab stops relative to the outer edge of the margin that is specified by fo:margin or fo:margin-left of the paragraph. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41755:•true: paragraph style determines the position of tab stops relative to the inner edge of the margin that is specified by fo:margin or fo:margin-left of the paragraph. Exception: the tab stop set by applied list style is determined by the paragraph style relative to the outer edge of the margin that is specified by fo:margin or fo:margin-left of the paragraph. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:41759:Note: In right-to-left layout environments, the paragraph's right margin is specified by fo:margin-left, and its tab stop positions are relative to the right edge.
